> Any affine toroidal family is a universal EGF family provided mild technical assumptions on the
> $(\Phi_i)_{i=1}^p$. (`main.tex:291`)

> An isometry spherical family is a universal EGF family, provided technical assumptions on the
> $(\Phi_i)_{i=1}^p$. (`main.tex:305`)

The corrected text of record (v2, `~/Dropbox/ErgodicGFN arXiv/source/main.tex`):

> An affine toroidal family is a universal EGF family provided its model realizes the uniform
> policy $\forwardalpha^i\equiv\frac1p$ and a set of outflows dense in the non-negative cone of
> $L^2(\Statespace,\lambda)$, and the group generated by the $(\Phi_i)_{i=1}^p$ acts ergodically on
> $(\mathbb T^d,\lambda)$; this holds when that group has no non-trivial invariant factor torus on
> which its linear part projects to an amenable group (Theorem 5 of \citet{bekka2015spectral}), and
