## SCOPE (disclosed)

Nothing is assumed beyond Mathlib: no named `Prop` is a hypothesis of a marked declaration. The
Bekka–Guivarc'h clause needs only "not ergodic ⇒ (ii)", a consequence of (i) ⇒ (ii) of their
Theorem 5, proved here directly by Fourier: an invariant indicator has a non-zero frequency whose
orbit under the transposed linear parts is finite (Parseval); its annihilator is a proper
invariant rational subspace on which the linear parts act through a finite group, hence
amenably. No group violating (ii) is exhibited for `d ≥ 1` (it needs the non-amenability of
`SL₂(ℤ)`). The other reading of C-54 (richness and ergodicity at different parameters) is false
and not formalized (C-54's finding); the "at every parameter" reading is implied. The sphere's
`λ` is `volume.toSphere`, `σ(A) = n · vol((0, 1) • A)`, the surface measure by polar coordinates;
Mathlib has no Riemannian volume to identify it with; it is the representation of
`EGF/SphereFamilies.lean`, not a reading. Continuity of the families is not encoded. The move counts (C-56):
two moves on `𝕋²` (`universality_tori_two_moves`), two rotations of `𝕊²` without their inverses
(`so3Pair`, `universality_sphere_two_moves_three`), one on `𝕊¹` (`universality_sphere_one_move`)
and on `𝕋¹` (`universality_tori_one_sqrt_two`); one move on `𝕋^d`, `d ≥ 2`, is
`EGF.exists_universality_tori_single_move` (cited, not restated). Not given: a pair generating a
dense subgroup of `SO(n)`, `n ≥ 4` (`breuillard2003dense`, not formalized).

Provenance: mathlib `fabf563a` (tag `v4.31.0`), pinned via `lakefile.toml`.
-/

